# Each entry here is a documented exception, not a silence. Every entry needs
# a comment explaining why the finding is not fixed yet and an `exp:` expiry
# date (trivy's native syntax) to force a revisit — an expired entry stops
# suppressing the finding and `mise run security` fails again until it is
# re-justified or the underlying version is bumped.

# CVE-2026-78661 — golang.org/x/net/html, found in /usr/local/bin/gh (#4).
# gh's go.sum resolves golang.org/x/net to v0.61.0 (below the v0.62.0 fix);
# no gh release has bumped past it yet. Unreachable in practice: gh never
# imports golang.org/x/net/html — confirmed with
# `go mod why golang.org/x/net/html` against github.com/cli/cli v2.104.0,
# which reports "main module does not need package golang.org/x/net/html".
# Revisit when gh bumps x/net, or sooner if a newer gh release is available.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2027-01-15

# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools 70.3.0, found only in pip's vendor manifest
# (/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt) (#66).
# The flaw is a path traversal in setuptools.package_index (PackageIndex
# download); pip vendors only pkg_resources from setuptools, not
# package_index, so the vulnerable code is not in the image (checked against
# the pip 26.3 wheel: no pip/_vendor/setuptools, only pip/_vendor/pkg_resources).
# Even pip 26.3 still lists setuptools==70.3.0. Revisit when pip bumps its
# vendored setuptools/pkg_resources.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-02-22
